86045585 true] [17592186399451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399451 1084 #uuid "0d45bd81-d2af-5d91-9d5a-2b641a8316e0" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399453 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1069 "q-162811" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1071 "Suppose we would like to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}z$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${y}^{2}+z=9$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,2yz,\\,{y}^{2}⟩=\\lambda ⟨\\boxed{}\\,, \\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨0,\\boxed{}\\,,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1 \\\\ {y}^{2}+z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1072 #uuid "8afa6e7b-08b3-5fd6-b960-921c9d4bc534" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399452 1074 "We need to find the maximum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}z\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1,\\,h(x,y,z)={y}^{2}+z=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=1 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2x,\\,2yz,\\,{y}^{2}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨2x,\\,0,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨0,\\,2y,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399454 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399455 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399456 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399457 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399458 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399456 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399453 1080 #uuid "9ec7c466-5f47-5c18-934e-2ba7c46ca3fb" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1081 "$y$ and $2z$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399454 1084 #uuid "4b59bf81-336b-5b77-a5ab-993e5da369cc" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1081 "$2$ and $y$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399455 1084 #uuid "cd2b1eac-ff7d-50ba-8e40-931f60aee6f6" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1081 "$2x$ and $2y$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399456 1084 #uuid "372a272b-dcaf-5ac5-a75d-2792619b147e" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1081 "$2x$ and $2z$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399457 1084 #uuid "92eb8681-34a4-5d3f-9b19-cabe81d62073" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399458 1081 "$2$ and $1$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399458 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399458 1084 #uuid "eda1895b-7d76-519b-8bab-824851119ae2" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399459 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399460 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399459 1069 "q-162812" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399459 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399459 1071 "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y-x=0$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩=\\lambda ⟨-1,\\boxed{}\\,, \\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\boxed{}\\,⟩ \\\\ y-x=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399459 1072 #uuid "5a114a88-7824-55e2-8ac4-08f991d5f004" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399459 1074 "We need to find the minimum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy+{z}^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)=y-x=0,\\,h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=0 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨y,\\,x,\\,2z⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨-1,\\,1,\\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,2z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399461 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399462 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399463 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399464 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399460 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399465 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399460 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 1319