4555" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1071 "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11=0.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1072 #uuid "84fd9eec-1cf5-594c-8917-00bf240277f1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399612 1074 "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+5({y}^{2}+4y)+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5([y+2)^{2}-4]+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5(y+2)^{2}-20+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399614 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399615 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399616 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399617 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399618 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399614 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399613 1080 #uuid "f0d3a90f-543b-5602-bf42-4796008282b3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1081 "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399614 1084 #uuid "ff8dd7e4-d04f-54e0-9c82-7503faa98408" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1081 "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,-2,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399615 1084 #uuid "6ee2009b-db2c-5ad5-a30f-47e82534faf3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1081 "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,2,1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399616 1084 #uuid "0eacccc9-5134-5c35-b00f-adda5251c8bd" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1081 "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(1,-2,0)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399617 1084 #uuid "1d5f9579-d5b4-564c-9ff2-31895a46959d" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1081 "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,2,1)$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399618 1084 #uuid "c2873b29-87cc-5f23-93ab-b79ab215b691" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399620 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1069 "q-16465" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1071 "For the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{20}=1$, find the lengths of its major and minor axes." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1072 #uuid "8cb21ae0-f2f0-5250-97c3-5094275c61e1" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399619 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-1$ and $k=-3,$ so the center is located at $(-1,-3).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=5$ and ${b}^{2}=20.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=5,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=20,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5}.$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399621 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399622 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399623 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399624 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399625 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1077 "selection" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399624 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399620 1080 #uuid "a9fd9c31-b922-5bc4-b3d4-983574117b6f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399621 1081 "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399621 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399621 1084 #uuid "e8434a84-5ef1-505b-a2c7-d42809c26959" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399622 1081 "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399622 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399622 1084 #uuid "386a0708-44f8-5648-9834-907d2d7fef7b" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1081 "$4$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399623 1084 #uuid "f019f459-9c8d-5bca-ac2e-8bf08a5f03f3" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399624 1081 "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399624 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399624 1084 #uuid "1362416b-6b2e-5b41-8cce-b430bb96c908" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399625 1081 "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{5}$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399625 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399625 1084 #uuid "c489543f-9ba5-563a-8700-e139b5d4d02f" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399627 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1069 "q-16642" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1071 "Calculate the points where the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1$ intercepts the $x$-axis." 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1072 #uuid "fca3c3f7-188d-5506-9818-be66c0607803" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399626 1074 "To calculate the $x$-intercept, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4}{9} & =1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2} & =20 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =\\frac{20}{9} \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{20}{9}} \\\\ x & =3\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at the points $(3-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0)$ and $(3+\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},0).$" 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399628 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399629 13194139533478 17592186045585 true] [17592186399627 1075 #edb/ref 17